    "body": "Follow-up to #36011\n\nWhen a connection handle outlives its signal, a callback that was still connected at signal destruction stays alive, and the handle continues to report `connected() == true`. The referenced PR fix made an explicit `disconnect()` call release the callback. However, destroying the signal still did not disconnect its callbacks automatically, as pointed out by the author in this [#36011 comment](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36011#discussion_r4459623066).\n\nThis PR's commit disconnects each callback when its signal is destroyed. It extends the `callback_destruction` test to verify that destroying the signal also releases an idle callback’s captured state and the surviving handle gets disconnected, as suggested in this [#36011 comment](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36011#discussion_r4459623272).",
