      "body": "I considered removing each `holder` from the vector before disconnecting it:\n\n```suggestion\n        while (!m_connections.empty()) {\n            auto holder{std::move(m_connections.back())};\n            m_connections.pop_back();\n```\n\nCodex suggested that if one of the callback's captures calls `connect()` on the same signal from its destructor, it can modify `m_connections` in-place, invalidating the for loop’s iterator. I haven’t seen an example of this happening in Bitcoin Core so I kept the loop.\n",
